Add `novelty` to the special-case handling alongside `mu`. For novelty, "improved" should mean the disagreement resolved (novelty and mu now agree), not that novelty increased. Alternatively, store the *direction* of expected improvement in `_remediation_state` when the remediation is applied, rather than hardcoding direction per metric name:
